  "notes": "The Exchange on 16th, 1800 Owens St -- formerly Dropbox's headquarters, now partly rebranded 'Icona: Labs at Mission Bay' -- a 750,370 sq ft, 12-story office/life-science campus on a ~3.5-acre lot, built by Kilroy Realty Corporation in 2018 as Dropbox's single-tenant headquarters (15-year lease). Sold in 2021 for $1.08B to KKR and Longfellow Real Estate Partners, who have since converted much of it to life-science labs; OpenAI signed a roughly 280,000 sq ft sublease reported closed Feb 2026. Blklot confirmed against the DataSF Assessor Historical Secured Property Tax Rolls dataset (wv5m-vpq2), whose property_location and square-footage/year-built fields match the published building exactly, since the base parcel map's own address field is a stale street-frontage number (701-707 16th St) rather than the building's current mailing address.",
